# Browser verification

- Do not open the browser, start a local server, or click through the UI to verify changes unless the user explicitly asks.
- After UI or logic changes, confirm the result from the edited source and stop.
- Do not treat browser tools, screenshots, or a full race walkthrough as required sign-off.
- If a check is needed without an explicit browser request, use a fast source check (read, grep). Do not spin up the app.
- Only use the browser when the user says to (for example “check in the browser” or “test it”).
